reachy-mini-cam-relay — Debian source notes
===========================================

This package is built with debhelper + dh-virtualenv. The application and
all of its Python dependencies (reachy-mini, pygobject, fastapi, ...) are
not available in Debian, so they are bundled into a self-contained
virtualenv installed under /opt/venvs/reachy-mini-cam-relay. The system
media libraries (GStreamer, v4l2loopback, PulseAudio) are shared with the
host and declared as Depends in debian/control.

Pinned dependencies
-------------------

The exact runtime dependency versions come from uv.lock (the single source
of truth). They are exported to debian/requirements.txt, which is NOT
committed — it is generated before each build:

    uv export --frozen --no-dev --no-annotate --no-hashes \
        --no-emit-project -o debian/requirements.txt

The helper script packaging/build-deb.sh does this for you.

Building locally
----------------

    ./packaging/build-deb.sh

Note: the bundled virtualenv is tied to the Python minor version of the
build host. To produce a package for Raspberry Pi OS / Debian 12 (python
3.11), build inside a debian:12 container (this is what CI does); see
.github/workflows/ci.yml.

Release version
---------------

The package is "3.0 (native)", so debian/changelog carries the bare
version (e.g. 0.1.0) with no Debian revision. On a release, CI sets that
version from multicz before building; the committed changelog only seeds
the entry.
